1
00:00:00,850 --> 00:00:04,530
The Vikings. Northern warriors who terrified Europe.

2
00:00:04,750 --> 00:00:08,460
It began on a quiet morning, in seven ninety-three.

3
00:00:08,550 --> 00:00:11,680
On Lindisfarne, the monks were reading in peace.

4
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:14,610
Suddenly, a ship appeared out of the mist.

5
00:00:15,500 --> 00:00:18,720
They crossed the North Sea, and nobody was ready.

6
00:00:19,300 --> 00:00:21,580
The monastery stood defenseless.

7
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:24,950
It was looted, and set on fire.

8
00:00:27,100 --> 00:00:31,210
The news shocked all of Europe. The Viking Age had begun.

9
00:00:32,700 --> 00:00:35,320
But why did they target monasteries?

10
00:00:36,900 --> 00:00:40,710
Because they held gold and silver, and had no soldiers.

11
00:00:41,700 --> 00:00:44,600
And then there's the myth of the horned helmet.

12
00:00:45,550 --> 00:00:48,230
No horned helmet has ever been found.

13
00:00:48,550 --> 00:00:52,620
It was made famous by an opera, in eighteen seventy-six.

14
00:00:52,700 --> 00:00:57,640
The Vikings sailed to England, France, Russia, and all the way to America.

15
00:00:59,300 --> 00:01:03,370
Next time: Ragnar Lothbrok. Legend, or reality?

